libtool 2.4.7: make libltdl's builtin-loader preloaded-symbols reference
weak.  Submitted by the Pizlix project.

Under Fil-C the standalone libltdl build is unshippable: ltdl.c declares
the never-defined data symbol `lt_libltdl_LTX_preloaded_symbols` extern
(it is only ever defined inside ltmain-generated convenience libraries
that link ltdl statically) and references it from lt_dlinit's
HAVE_LIBDLLOADER block.  The Fil-C compiler routes that reference through
a pizlonated_ forwarder, so the built /usr/lib/libltdl.so carries a
NON-WEAK undefined reference to `pizlonated_lt_libltdl_LTX_preloaded_
symbols`, which (a) makes every -lltdl link of an EXECUTABLE fail at link
time (the reference cannot be resolved from the executable), and (b)
would make every load of the library fail at runtime.  With the reference
weak, the reference resolves to NULL exactly as the dynamic-loader case
always intended: lt_dlpreload(NULL) is the documented "clear the preloaded
list" path (loaders/preopen.c:315 guards the NULL and falls back to its
own default_preloaded_symbols), so behavior of the standalone library is
unchanged -- the builtin loader vtable still gets installed, and nothing
ever depended on the symbol being non-NULL in a standalone libltdl.

diff --git a/libltdl/ltdl.c b/libltdl/ltdl.c
--- a/libltdl/ltdl.c
+++ b/libltdl/ltdl.c
@@ -219,7 +219,15 @@
 LT_BEGIN_C_DECLS
 LT_SCOPE const lt_dlvtable *	get_vtable (lt_user_data data);
 LT_END_C_DECLS
 #ifdef HAVE_LIBDLLOADER
-extern LT_DLSYM_CONST lt_dlsymlist preloaded_symbols[];
+/* Fil-C: this list is only ever DEFINED inside ltmain-generated
+   convenience libraries that link ltdl statically; the standalone
+   libltdl build has always shipped an undefined reference here.  The
+   fil-C compiler routes the reference through a pizlonated_ forwarder,
+   which made the shared library unshippable (a hard undefined symbol
+   poisons every executable link and every load).  Declare it weak: the
+   reference then resolves to NULL, which is exactly what lt_dlpreload
+   (loaders/preopen.c) already handles -- "clear the preloaded list".  */
+extern LT_DLSYM_CONST lt_dlsymlist preloaded_symbols[] __attribute__((__weak__));
 #endif

 /* Initialize libltdl. */
